    "introduction": "GSK develops vaccines and prescription medicines used to prevent and treat disease in markets around the world. Its activities cover specialty medicines, vaccines and established treatments, including work in respiratory disease, immunology, oncology and HIV. Customers ultimately include healthcare systems and patients, with medicines reaching them through regulated distribution and reimbursement arrangements. Revenue from approved products supports research, clinical trials and manufacturing investment. The company must demonstrate safety and clinical effectiveness before launching treatments and continue monitoring them afterwards. Its business is shaped by the strength of its development pipeline, access to healthcare budgets, manufacturing reliability and the loss of exclusivity as products mature.",
